    <!-- THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT. A comment placed ABOVE
         <FlexiPage> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with the misleading "unable to
         find matching parent xml file" error.

         ONE DISPOSITION ENTRY ADDED 2026-08-10 (code review 3B/3C, C3). The pre-existing
         acquisition entry is UNTOUCHED, byte for byte, and nothing else on this page changed.

         ⚠ DYNAMIC ACTIONS WAS ALREADY ON HERE (enableActionsConfiguration = true) AND WAS NOT
         ENABLED ANYWHERE NEW. Turning it on where it is OFF silently EMPTIES that page's
         action bar by discarding every inherited action, which cost three pages their buttons
         in this repo. This edit only appends one entry to a list that already existed.

         =====================================================================
         WHY THE PAGE NEEDED THIS: D20/C1 FOR THE THIRD TIME.
         =====================================================================
         The single pre-existing entry is gated on {!$User.Deal_Driver__c} EQUAL true. A
         disposition driver holds Disposition_Deal_Driver, which grants FLS on
         User.Disposition_Driver__c and NOT on User.Deal_Driver__c, and a flexipage visibility
         rule that reads a field the running user cannot read evaluates FALSE. Since this list
         IS the whole action bar, a disposition driver saw NO BUTTONS AT ALL on a sell-side
         PSA, and 3C's entire gate split (RecordStageAdvanceService's Disposition_PSA ->
         DISPOSITION_DRIVER config, pinned both ways by
         RecordStageAdvanceServiceTest.contractReviewGateIsResolvedPerRecordTypeNotPerObject)
         had no UI that could invoke it. Same shape closed on NDA_Record_Page (3A fix pass) and
         LOI_Record_Page (3B, D22).

         =====================================================================
         THIS IS THE DUPLICATE-ENTRY SHAPE, NOT AN OR. DO NOT MERGE THE TWO.
         =====================================================================
         A flexipage booleanFilter has no negation operator, and this repo has MEASURED that a
         parenthesised OR ('1 AND (2 OR 3)') deploys, survives a retrieve, and is STILL NOT
         HONOURED BY THE RENDERER. Two valueListItems carrying the same <value> is the shape
         NDA_Record_Page introduced and LOI_Record_Page repeated. ⚠ Its deploy-and-render gate
         is INHERITED here, not re-proven: confirm at check-only that duplicate <value> entries
         are accepted, and confirm in the org that a user holding BOTH driver flags does not
         see Advance Stage rendered twice.

         =====================================================================
         THE SECOND CRITERION IS COPIED VERBATIM, AND UNLIKE THE LOI CASE THAT IS SAFE.
         =====================================================================
         D22 refused to copy LOI_Record_Page's entry because its second criterion read
         Is_Advance_Allowed__c, an ACQUISITION-SHAPED formula that excluded only `Completed`
         and therefore returned TRUE at `Executed`, the DISPOSITION terminal stage. Copying it
         then would have rendered a button on a finished disposition LOI.

         THAT DEFECT SHAPE DOES NOT EXIST HERE, and it was checked rather than assumed:
           - Contract_Review__c has NO Is_Advance_Allowed__c formula field at all. The gate is
             the inline criterion Negotiation_Status__c NE 'Executed'.
           - BOTH record types expose the SAME four Negotiation_Status__c values (Initial Draft,
             Revised, Ready for Execution, Executed) - Acquisition_PSA and Disposition_PSA both
             state that this identity is deliberate.
           - CONTRACT_REVIEW_NEXT_STAGE maps Initial Draft => Revised => Ready for Execution =>
             Executed and stops. `Executed` is the ONLY terminal, and it is the same terminal on
             both types, so a single NE test names every terminal there is.
         There is therefore no second terminal for this criterion to miss. If a future change
         gives either type a status the other lacks, this criterion and CONTRACT_REVIEW_NEXT_STAGE
         must be revisited together.

         =====================================================================
         NO RECORD-TYPE CRITERION ON EITHER ENTRY, AND HERE THAT IS A DIFFERENT ARGUMENT
         FROM LOI_Record_Page'S.
         =====================================================================
         On LOI__c the two Stage__c value sets are DISJOINT, so a stage-keyed rule is
         self-limiting to its own record type. That mechanism is NOT available on this object -
         the two PSA value sets are IDENTICAL, so no status value discriminates. The
         discriminator here is the DRIVER FLAG alone, which is sufficient because the two flags
         are granted by disjoint permission sets. The residual is the same cosmetic one
         NDA_Record_Page and LOI_Record_Page accept: an acquisition driver opening a disposition
         PSA still sees Advance Stage and gets a refusal from RecordStageAdvanceService's
         record-type-scoped gate. Nothing here can write what the server would refuse -
         RecordStageAdvanceController asserts the gate regardless of what this page renders.

         ⚠ DEPLOY GATE, NOT SATISFIED BY THIS FILE: the rule is only EVALUABLE if the running
         user has FLS read on User.Disposition_Driver__c. That grant lives in
         Disposition_Deal_Driver; if a persona reaches this page without that set in their PSG
         the rule evaluates FALSE and the button is invisible again, silently.
    -->
    <flexiPageRegions>
        <itemInstances>
            <componentInstance>
                <componentInstanceProperties>
                    <name>actionNames</name>
                    <valueList>
                        <valueListItems>
                            <value>Contract_Review__c.Advance_Stage</value>
                            <visibilityRule>
                                <booleanFilter>1 AND 2</booleanFilter>
                                <criteria>
                                    <leftValue>{!$User.Deal_Driver__c}</leftValue>
                                    <operator>EQUAL</operator>
                                    <rightValue>true</rightValue>
                                </criteria>
                                <criteria>
                                    <leftValue>{!Record.Negotiation_Status__c}</leftValue>
                                    <operator>NE</operator>
                                    <rightValue>Executed</rightValue>
                                </criteria>
                            </visibilityRule>
                        </valueListItems>
                        <valueListItems>
